Twenty-nine programs hand-ported from the Roc language's own test suite, each
frozen with the value the original Roc program produces. ROC IS THE ORACLE:
every .expected is Roc's answer, never generated by a compiler of ours.

SOURCE
  roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig
  ~100+ snippets in that file; 29 ported so far. Each unit's own prose names
  the exact case it came from and any adaptation made (Codex prints an Integer
  where Roc prints a Float, a thunk takes an ignored argument because Codex has
  no nullary function type, a tag carries named fields because Codex has no
  anonymous record). The value is what survives every adaptation.

PORTED ON
  NewRepository branch roc-ports-batch2 (commit e0595f3f, 2026-08-27), before
  the Rust compiler existed. roc-ports-type-recovery holds 11 of these 29,
  byte-identical -- a themed subset, not a second version.

RESOLVED AT
  cobblestone-u58 (8570fba1, the U58 candidate) with the Rust `bundle`. Each
  unit here is self-contained: the cited Foreword chapters are inlined and the
  readable port sits at the end. Re-cut from the same source if a later Update
  moves what these exercise.

ORACLE SPOT-CHECK (against the Roc source, not just past work)
  fold-product 24, fold-sum 10, alias-list 6, closure-captures-list "captured"
  all match Roc's own asserted results (modulo the Integer/Float format note).

WHAT THE ARMS FIND
  run-interp.sh (Rust interpreter) and run-wasm.sh (wasm plug) produce Roc's
  answer for all 29. run-zig.sh does NOT: 23 compile and match, 6 fail to
  compile, because the zig plug demands concrete types the interpreter and the
  wasm plug do not. Those 6 are the corpus earning its keep:

    unresolved type var   roc-iter-map, roc-iter-keep-if, roc-iter-drop-if
      The polymorphic map/keep/drop leaves a type variable the zig plug cannot
      resolve. These are also the three that differ under ir-irdump.sh (irdump
      spells the variable 45, codexir 16). The frontend accepts the program --
      a type-changing probe types cleanly on both -- and the interpreter and
      wasm plug run it; the strict zig backend is what shows the residual
      variable matters. NOT benign, as an earlier note here wrongly said.

    no element type       roc-alias-empty
      An empty list's element type is left unresolved.

    pointless discard     roc-alias-original, roc-list-called-twice
      The zig plug emits a discard for a local it also uses -- an aliasing
      codegen fault, in exactly the sharing question these ports were chosen to
      ask.

  Whether each is an upstream frontend gap (a type left unresolved) or a
  zig-plug fault (bad codegen) is the next investigation. The zig arm uses
  codexzig -- upstream's frontend and zig plug -- so all six are upstream's.
